# Third-party repos. Ignored BY DEFAULT, vendored only by explicit opt-in below.
# This ordering is deliberate: LIBERO ships ~100 GB of demonstration data, and a
# blanket un-ignore of external/ would try to commit it. Add a negation per repo,
# never a blanket one. Hashes recorded in context/SETUP.md.
external/*
!external/README.md
# Diffusion Policy is VENDORED (decision 2026-07-29): committed in full at
# upstream commit 5ba07ac6661db573af695b419a7947ecb704690f. MIT licensed;
# LICENSE file is included in the vendored tree as that license requires.
!external/diffusion_policy/

# Raw experiment output — the source of truth and the only irreplaceable
# artifact in this project. (Parent dirs must be re-included explicitly or git
# never descends into them to see the negation.)
#
# Top-level *.jsonl IS committed (changed 2026-07-29). Table A is per-episode and
# costs ~660 bytes/row — the full Phase-2 grid (~6750 episodes) projects to only
# ~4.4 MB, so there is no reason not to have it browsable and diffable in git.
#
# Per-STEP tables (Table B) are a different scale: ~1.35M rows ≈ 200 MB at the
# full grid. Those must NOT be committed raw — write them to logs/steps/ (already
# covered by logs/*) and rely on the gzipped archive below.
logs/*
!logs/README.md
!logs/*.jsonl
!logs/archive/
logs/archive/*
!logs/archive/*.jsonl.gz
!logs/archive/*.csv.gz
!logs/archive/MANIFEST.md

data/
outputs/
wandb/

# Checkpoints
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
checkpoints/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/

# Secrets
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store
